From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:30:25 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: return buffers queued before a failed start as
 QUEUED

vb2_start_streaming() hands the queued buffers to buf_queue() before it
calls start_streaming(). When the instance is already in the error state,
iris_vb2_buf_queue() completed each of them with VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR, so
they sat on the done list when iris_vb2_start_streaming() then failed with
-EBUSY, and vb2 warned:

  qcom-iris 5a00000.video-codec: session error for command: 3007001,
  event id:1007
  WARNING: drivers/media/common/videobuf2/videobuf2-core.c:1821 at
  vb2_start_streaming+0xdc/0x180, CPU#5: ffmpeg/5354

Seen when the firmware rejected an encoder session after STREAMON on the
OUTPUT queue and userspace then started the CAPTURE queue.

Before start_streaming() has been called, put the buffer on the m2m queue
instead; start_streaming() fails on the error state and returns it with
VB2_BUF_STATE_QUEUED, as vb2 requires.

Tested on a MANGMI Air X (SM6115) with the trigger above: the same
session error now fails the CAPTURE STREAMON with -EBUSY and no warning.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
index 8faf709c26c1..620d83642d94 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vb2.c
@@ -300,6 +300,11 @@ void iris_vb2_buf_queue(struct vb2_buffer *vb2)
 
 	mutex_lock(&inst->lock);
 	if (inst->state == IRIS_INST_ERROR) {
+		/* Before start_streaming, which fails and returns it as QUEUED */
+		if (!vb2_start_streaming_called(vb2->vb2_queue)) {
+			v4l2_m2m_buf_queue(inst->m2m_ctx, vbuf);
+			goto exit;
+		}
 		ret = -EBUSY;
 		goto exit;
 	}
